Even though I am standing under the shade of my office building, I can still feel some drops of rain hitting. It's literally hitting me. I have been waiting for my cab for almost 10 mins. As I am waiting, on the other side of the road I see a couple walking. The lady is walking with her left arm spread, her husband on the other hand is probably fussing over her it seems as he has a frown on his face and mumbling while trying to tug her hands in. She finally stops and let him pull her hands towards himself and wipe them with his sleeves. She giggles looking at him to which the man sigh and just smiles. Whatching this scene even I let a smile slip.

Suddenly, a yellow cab stops infront of me cutting me off. From the drivers seat a man bellowed "Miss. Annie? You had booked a taxi to Star building?". I rush forward moving my hand to my head to shelter my head and answer "Yes yes thats me."

I start rumaging through my bag for my phone murmuring about checking the code. Interrupting me he said "No need Maam. Get in". I paused looking up at him. "Why? Don't you need a code to confirm?" I ask confused. 

He replied urgently "It got cancelled cause i was late. Now please get in my seat is getting wet." Hmmm. I was not aware of anything like that. I moved towards the passenger door slowly still in doubt and hesitating. 

"Do you want to go or not? Its raining like cats & dogs you won't get another cab here anyways." He was right as I couldn't see any vehicle nor any person. This street is not very buzy but is also not very quiet like it seemed now. I muttered  fine then got inside the cab. 

As soon as I closed the door he slammed on the gas and tore down the street. Slowly I let out a breath. I reached inside my bag for a small cloth that I have a habit of keeping and dabbed myself. Just then I heard a notification sound from my bag. I started digging through my bag for my phone. After a few seconds, I felt a cold box like object in side the bag which I pulled out. "Finally" I whispered out in relief clutching my phone like a treasure. 

I  open my phone to see what the notification was about. As soon as I read the message, a chill runs down my spine. 

Text message:
Unknown: Sorry, running 10 minutes late, I'm pulling up to your location now.

Terrified, I drag my eyes away from my screen and look up. No no. It must be a mistake. But he said my name. He was very sure. 

Staring at the back of his head, I open my mouth trying to say something but fear seals my throat. I close my eyes and take a deep breath then open my eyes again. Finally mustering up some strength i ask, "Who are you? Where are you taking me?" 

He answers without turning back "What do you mean Maam? I am taking you to your place. Star Building." I processed what he said then looked around. Only now I realize we are on an unfamiliar street. 

I stare at him, unblinking. I am  terrified. I want to scream. But I remain calm. Now I am very sure something is wrong. 

"Where are you taking me? I don't think this street leads to my place. In fact I don't remember mentioning in the app about Star Building being my place." I say watching him for any kind of reaction. 

I am very sure no one is supposed to know about it being anyone's place unless being told so. Because it wasn't until recently. Star building was used for commercial purposes. Few months before it was changed and then rented out. Not many people know that. 

He didn't react to it at all. "Stop the car. I want to get down here." He stopped the car. 

I blinked in surprise. He had actually listened. I grabbed my bag, my left hand on the door handle ready to get down. Suddenly he turned around and sprayed something on my face. I started coughing. Then a sudden dizziness washed over me. 

"W-what...d-did...you...do??" I mumbled, the words heavy on my tongue. He didn't reply. Instead I felt the car seat shaking and vibrating. Then everything went dark.
